# The build context is the repo root, because the Dockerfile needs both ingest/
# and deploy/docker/. Everything below would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon
# on every build.

# The single biggest one: node_modules is ~500 MB and the image has no Node
# stage, so it is pure upload cost.
dashboard/node_modules/
dashboard/.next/
# dashboard/out is NOT excluded... except it is also not used: the build reads
# the committed copy at ingest/internal/mock/web. Excluding it keeps the context
# honest about what actually goes in.
dashboard/out/

# The extracts. 1.8 GB of CSV that is mounted at runtime, never built in.
data/*.csv
*.csv

# Build output and local state.
ingest/bin/
.git/
.claude/
.gstack/

# Secrets, belt and braces. .env is gitignored too, but a build context is a
# separate mechanism and this file is the only thing standing between a local
# .env and a layer in the image.
.env
*.env
!*.env.example
deploy/librechat/data-node/
deploy/librechat/images/
deploy/librechat/uploads/
deploy/librechat/logs/

# Docs and artefacts that cannot affect a build.
docs/
pitch/
prototype/
*.md
!README.md
